<title>POLAND: Poland raises drug prices by 13 pct from July 1.</title>
<headline>Poland raises drug prices by 13 pct from July 1.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish finance ministry said in a statement on Thursday it will raise official prices of domestically produced drugs subsidised by the state by an average of 13 percent from July 1.</p>
<p>The rise, affecting about 30 percent of drugs with prices controlled by the government, is in line with the schedule envisaged by the 1996 budget.</p>
<p>Earlier this year the health ministry said the government would likely free drug prices in 1998, which may lift them by about 40 percent. The move is seen as necessary to complete the pharmaceutical sector's privatisation.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700'</p>
</text>
